      "message": "registerAudioGainCallback.\n\nAlso, I understand that the IAudioGainCallback can be implemented by the IAudioGain interface and access by other components than the audio server. Why does it need to be registered by the audio server via the IPrimaryDevice API? I did not see how it is used by the audio framework. Is there a CL for that?\n\nAlso, if it is needed by the audio framework, why limit it to IPrimaryDevice and not add it to IDevice interface?",
