      "lineNbr": 79,
      "author": {
        "id": 1042638
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-02-03T21:37:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Audio HAL doesn\u0027t support more than one client, and that client is usually the audio framework.  Also, since the result of \u0027openPrimaryDevice\u0027 is not stored anywhere, the returned client interface will automatically vanish after exiting this method, and the audio HAL service can close the device.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 69,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 79,
        "endChar": 0
      },
      "revId": "782f4cc8d19b0e026849cb8def58651584192ec9",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "749139ed_1e0c9d4f",
        "filename": "audio/audiogain/all-versions/default/AudioGain.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 8
      },
      "lineNbr": 79,
      "author": {
        "id": 1491204
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-02-08T13:10:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Excellent remark. We\u0027v been facing this kind of issue since IAudioControl automotive interface has been introduced and highly recommanded to be implemented by primary HAL.\nAs a result, we have 2 clients for a while in AudioHAL.\n\nAudio HAL Primary Device IF has been \"singletonized\" within our DeviceFactory.cpp.",
      "parentUuid": "da9c32b6_914484ef",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 69,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 79,
        "endChar": 0
      },
      "revId": "782f4cc8d19b0e026849cb8def58651584192ec9",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
